// Pennsylvania's own Grade 4 social studies units (`pa-g4-` ids): Pennsylvania studies. Chapter 4 of the Pennsylvania
// Code asks every elementary student to study the history of the Commonwealth, geography and civics at least once, and
// Pennsylvania's standards repeat each area at every grade, so Grade 4 is the year the course is about Pennsylvania: its
// first peoples, William Penn and the colony, Philadelphia and the founding of the nation, its government, symbols,
// land, cities, industry, the fight over slavery and the Civil War, immigration and work, markets and money. Native
// nations are named as peoples historically tied to the land, with the nations that exist today described in the present
// tense (their governments and communities are in Oklahoma, Wisconsin, New York and elsewhere); nothing sacred or
// ceremonial is asked about. Slavery, removal, unfair land deals and dangerous work are told plainly and factually.

